export anchor EarthyProfessionalStyle:
    number: 221
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Earthy professional
    idea: A serious, grounded workspace in olive, sand and clay, with a dark olive sidebar, serif figures set like a ledger and projects filed under their departments.
    base: light
    palette:
        sand: #f1ebdf, the page
        paper: #fbf8f1, cards, fields and the style sheet
        olive: #33391f, the sidebar
        oliveMid: #4b5330, the current nav item
        olivePrimary: #4f5a26, the primary button
        sandText: #ece4cf, text on the sidebar
        clay: #a85a33, progress lines, this week bars and the mark, never small text
        clayInk: #8c4423, department labels, links and the focus ring
        clayTint: #f3e2d4, the overdue notice and the focus halo
        ink: #2a2620, text and figures
        ink2: #5a5244, secondary text and labels
        line: #ddd2bb, rules and card edges
        edge: #8f8166, field borders and the ledger double rule
        green: #2f6b34, On track with an outlined circle and check
        amber: #875700, At risk with an outlined triangle and bang
        red: #a1221f, Behind with an outlined square and down arrow, and overdue
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings, figures and project names use Iowan Old
        Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Charter, Georgia.
        Text and labels use Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
        Arial. The greeting is 38px serif 500, ledger figures 46px serif,
        section titles 24px serif, project names 17px serif 600, caps
        labels 12px tracked 0.14em, body 14px sans.
    layout:
        A 240px dark olive sidebar runs the full height. It holds a clay
        disc mark with the serif brand, a small Workspace caption, the six
        nav items with thin line icons where the current one has a lighter
        olive fill and a clay left bar, and the signed in user Mara Okafor
        pinned at the bottom. The main area starts with a row holding a
        wide search field at left and an olive New project button and a
        square bell at right, over a rule. The greeting has the date as a
        small caps eyebrow over Good day, Mara in serif, with a clay edged
        notice at right reading 4 tasks are overdue and need attention
        first. The KPIs are a ledger, four columns under a double rule and
        over a single rule, split by thin vertical rules, each a large
        serif figure, a caps label and a short note. Below are two
        columns. The wider left is Projects by department, with clay caps
        headings for Design, Engineering, Research and Marketing, and under
        each a row with the serif name, the percent and tasks, the status
        and the due date with days left, and a thin clay line for progress
        across the row foot. The right column holds a paper card titled
        Week over week with seven day rows of paired horizontal bars, last
        week sand with an outline above this week clay, the two values at
        the row end and totals below, then a recent activity card with
        small clay diamonds on a vertical rule. Below 1100px the columns
        stack. Below 860px the sidebar becomes a top band with the nav
        scrolling sideways and the ledger goes two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page padding and column gap, 12 to 14px row padding.
    density: Medium. Rows read like a ledger, grouped under department labels.
    corners: Small, 4px on cards, buttons and fields. Only the avatar is round.
    borders: 1px line rules. A 3px double rule tops the ledger and the style sheet.
    shadows: None. Surfaces separate by sand against paper.
    icons:
        18px line icons at 1.6px stroke. Status icons are 15px outlined
        shapes, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bang and a square
        with a down arrow. Activity uses small clay outlined diamonds on a
        rule.
    focus: A 2px clayInk outline offset 2px with a 5px clayTint halo, and a sand outline in the sidebar.
    tone: Measured and formal, such as Good day, Mara, Need attention first and Week over week.
